WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.287
A signal leaves node 0 and the roads have different costs.

00:07.287 --> 00:14.700
Walking every route repeats the same roads again and again.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.264
Keep a heap of arrival times.

00:20.264 --> 00:31.700
The smallest one can’t be beaten, so that node’s time is final.

00:32.000 --> 00:43.214
Going through node 1 reaches node 2 at time 3, which beats the direct road of 4.

00:43.214 --> 00:47.700
A cheaper road updates the time.

00:48.000 --> 00:53.850
Each road is checked once, so it’s O(E log V).

00:53.850 --> 00:57.665
The last node hears at time 7.

00:57.665 --> 00:59.700
That’s Dijkstra.
